<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
{#
  The `<?xml ...?>` declaration above must be the very first thing this
  file writes -- see sitemap.njk's own comment on this same point.

  A syndication feed of the editions -- not of every page this
  site generates. Its item universe is `events` (site/src/_data/
  events.json) directly, so the archive index, its year and filter pages,
  and the three other static pages are excluded by construction: none of
  them is an edition, so none of them was ever a candidate. Unlike the
  sitemap above, which makes an explicit, commented decision to leave two
  archive pages out, this file makes no such decision -- the question
  never arises here.

  Every edition is listed, upcoming and past alike, newest first
  (`sort(true, false, 'date')` -- `events.json`'s own dates are always
  `YYYY-MM-DD`, so a lexicographic sort is already a chronological one,
  not because the fixture happens to be pre-sorted): an upcoming edition
  is exactly the kind of thing a subscriber to this feed wants to learn
  about first. Zero events (a wholly empty `events.json`) renders a
  channel with no `<item>` at all -- a valid, empty feed, not an error.

  `pubDate` comes from the edition's own `date` (the `rfc822` filter,
  site/.eleventy.js) -- never `new Date()` read at build time, which would
  make every rebuild churn this feed for a reason that has nothing to do
  with its actual content, exactly the failure `parisToday()`/
  `paris_today` exists to rule out on the Python side of this project.

  An edition with no `abstract` yet falls back to naming its speaker --
  `event | eventDescription` (site/.eleventy.js), the one rule event.njk's
  own `pageDescription` and structured-data block call too, so the two
  cannot state the description of the same edition two different ways.
  They once did; this filter is what closed it.
#}
<rss version="2.0">
<channel>
<title>{{ site.title }}</title>
<link>{{ '/' | absoluteUrl }}</link>
<description>{{ site.tagline }}</description>
{%- for e in events | sort(true, false, 'date') %}
{%- set itemUrl = ('/events/' ~ (e.id | lower) ~ '/') | absoluteUrl %}
{%- set itemDescription = e | eventDescription %}
<item>
<title>{{ e.title }}</title>
<link>{{ itemUrl }}</link>
<guid isPermaLink="true">{{ itemUrl }}</guid>
<pubDate>{{ e.date | rfc822 }}</pubDate>
<description>{{ itemDescription }}</description>
</item>
{%- endfor %}
</channel>
</rss>
